    "en": "The University of Abomey-Calavi (UAC) is the largest and most important institution of higher education in Benin. Founded in 1970, it has grown into a vast campus that attracts tens of thousands of students from Benin and neighboring countries. The UAC offers a wide range of degree programs in the humanities, social sciences, natural sciences, and engineering. It is a crucial center for research and innovation in West Africa and plays an essential role in training the country's future elite. The campus itself is a small city with faculty buildings, libraries, student dormitories, and sports facilities, forming the intellectual heart of Benin."
